Subject: [PATCH] SukiSU: initialize SUSFS domain SIDs on legacy kernels

The pre-5.10 policy path reset the AVC but never populated the SUSFS SID
cache. The separate cache_sid() call only fills the core KSU cache, leaving
SUSFS domain comparisons against zero. This breaks zygote child handling,
manager fd installation, mount tagging and the sdcard monitor on 4.19.

Resolve the SIDs after releasing the policy write lock (or stop_machine)
and resetting the AVC, matching the ordering of the newer policy path.
SID resolution may take the policy read lock, so it must remain outside
the write-side critical section.

diff --git a/kernel/selinux/rules.c b/kernel/selinux/rules.c
--- a/kernel/selinux/rules.c
+++ b/kernel/selinux/rules.c
@@ -257,6 +257,9 @@ do_stop_machine:
 out_flush:
     smp_mb();
     reset_avc_cache();
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS
+    susfs_set_batch_sid();
+#endif
 #endif
 }
 
